WEBVTT

01:49.109 --> 01:56.116
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE

01:59.244 --> 02:00.995
FOR THE INDEPENDENCE OF KOREA

02:03.706 --> 02:05.041
In two weeks' time…

02:05.625 --> 02:09.462
…a fundraiser will be held at Bumingwan
for the Frontline General Rally.

02:09.546 --> 02:13.174
After Tokyo's bombing, the Japanese Army
planned a propaganda event

02:13.258 --> 02:17.637
to exploit our resources and deploy
more Joseon men to the front lines.

02:18.471 --> 02:22.225
It will be a fundraising party
to procure money for that rally.

02:22.308 --> 02:24.978
Lieutenant General Minami,
Lieutenant General Seijiro,

02:25.061 --> 02:26.146
Major General Junji,

02:26.938 --> 02:30.108
Police Chief Nishimura,
and Commissioner Ishikawa will be there,

02:30.191 --> 02:32.610
as will all the big names in Gyeongseong.

02:34.320 --> 02:36.739
Jin Seon-jung of the United Society
and Park Yong-su

02:36.823 --> 02:39.367
of the People's Livelihood Corps
will also be attending.

02:40.326 --> 02:44.080
It will be a momentous occasion.
Make sure to attend it.

02:47.959 --> 02:50.879
So, the leaders
of the Japanese occupation forces

02:50.962 --> 02:54.799
and the heads of the pro-Japanese traitors
will all be gathered in one place.

02:56.718 --> 02:58.887
This will be
the chance of a lifetime for us.

02:58.970 --> 03:01.431
We have about 20 kilograms
of dynamite we swiped

03:01.514 --> 03:04.350
when we were planning to explode
the Han River railway.

03:05.268 --> 03:09.063
We had to abort the plan
when Comrade Jeong Seung-jong got caught,

03:10.273 --> 03:11.858
but we still have the dynamite.

03:12.775 --> 03:15.778
It's imperative that we don't get caught
before the rebellion.

03:16.988 --> 03:18.573
Don't worry, Comrade Kwon.

03:19.073 --> 03:20.658
Only I know the location

03:22.035 --> 03:22.952
of the explosives.

03:31.294 --> 03:32.629
Run!

03:49.479 --> 03:50.480
Move it!

03:52.440 --> 03:53.441
Comrade Kwon.

03:57.862 --> 04:00.531
Comrade Lee In-hyeok? How did this happen?

04:01.366 --> 04:02.909
For handing out seditious flyers.

04:03.993 --> 04:06.829
And strangely, he's being taken
not to Seodaemun Prison, but…

04:06.913 --> 04:08.039
But?

04:08.122 --> 04:09.707
…to Ongseong Hospital.

04:33.106 --> 04:34.023
Look here!

04:36.693 --> 04:41.614
LONG LIVE THE EMPEROR
DEVOTE ALL TO WAR

04:54.377 --> 04:55.461
Comrade Lee?

04:55.545 --> 04:56.546
Who are you?

04:58.006 --> 04:59.966
- Are you a Joseon-born?
- Excuse me.

05:00.049 --> 05:02.051
Hey!

05:04.846 --> 05:06.389
Help us, sir.

05:06.472 --> 05:08.141
Please help us get out of here.

05:09.559 --> 05:10.727
Do you know Lee In-hyeok?

05:10.810 --> 05:13.688
I have a three-year-old
and a five-year-old at home.

05:14.480 --> 05:17.150
They must've been starving
for days. Please.

05:18.067 --> 05:22.238
Please help me get back home. Please?

05:22.322 --> 05:25.700
Forgive me.
I'm on a more urgent mission right now.

05:26.576 --> 05:27.785
Sir, please.

05:27.869 --> 05:30.371
Hey! Over here!

05:30.872 --> 05:31.873
Here!

05:32.582 --> 05:33.583
- I'm sorry.
- Sir!

05:38.087 --> 05:39.088
Comrade Kwon!

05:39.589 --> 05:41.174
You came all this way…

05:42.050 --> 05:45.261
Now, come on. Get us out of here.

05:47.597 --> 05:49.432
I'm afraid I don't have time.

05:49.515 --> 05:50.683
What do you mean?

05:51.893 --> 05:53.728
Aren't you here to free us?

05:54.771 --> 05:56.647
Tell me where you hid the dynamite.

05:57.690 --> 06:00.151
We have less than ten days left
until the rebellion.

06:00.234 --> 06:02.403
We cannot waste this precious opportunity!

06:03.404 --> 06:06.657
Tell me where you hid the dynamite,
Comrade Lee.

06:07.909 --> 06:08.910
No.

06:10.453 --> 06:11.704
Free us first.

06:13.706 --> 06:15.625
I can't afford to do that right now.

06:15.708 --> 06:18.336
First, tell me where the dynamite is.

06:19.670 --> 06:21.297
I promise, as soon as I get out,

06:22.006 --> 06:24.175
I will find a way to free you two.

06:25.093 --> 06:26.511
Freeing us comes first.

06:26.594 --> 06:27.512
Comrade Lee!

06:27.595 --> 06:28.596
Listen!

06:29.305 --> 06:30.807
This place is a living hell!

06:32.141 --> 06:33.768
This isn't an ordinary prison!

06:36.646 --> 06:39.524
Comrade Kwon,
if we don't get out of this place…

06:42.652 --> 06:43.736
you'll get no dynamite.

06:47.657 --> 06:48.741
Don't move.

06:49.492 --> 06:50.827
Hands above your head!

10:09.775 --> 10:11.902
What on Earth was that thing?

10:12.695 --> 10:16.282
I don't know what it is,
but I'm sure it was created here.

11:30.773 --> 11:33.234
First, let's get out of this place.

11:33.317 --> 11:37.196
There is a way to reach the central vent
behind this boiler room.

11:37.279 --> 11:38.280
Let's head that way.

12:41.260 --> 12:42.094
Drop your weapon.

12:45.014 --> 12:46.474
Did you not hear me?!

12:47.266 --> 12:48.559
Drop your knife.

13:04.366 --> 13:07.703
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE
BETWEEN DENIAL AND TRUTH

13:07.787 --> 13:10.372
EPISODE 5
DESPERATION

13:11.332 --> 13:12.917
I said drop your knife!

13:17.421 --> 13:20.007
For now, let's do what he says.

13:21.008 --> 13:22.843
And what, die here in vain?

13:22.927 --> 13:25.930
I'm saying let's not get carried away
by ill-advised bravery.

13:26.555 --> 13:30.392
Not only are you quick to compromise,
but also quick to give up.

13:30.476 --> 13:32.019
Call it quick judgment.

13:32.728 --> 13:34.980
The ability to deal with crises

13:35.981 --> 13:37.066
flexibly.

13:39.777 --> 13:41.779
I can't believe you're laughing.

13:42.363 --> 13:44.323
At least we escaped the creature.

13:44.907 --> 13:45.991
I'm not so sure.

13:47.618 --> 13:49.286
I wonder which creature is worse.

13:50.162 --> 13:51.580
This is your final warning.

13:52.456 --> 13:54.875
Drop your knife right now!

14:10.224 --> 14:13.686
To die so recklessly
means to lose against them.

14:14.186 --> 14:15.020
Drop it.

14:15.729 --> 14:17.731
Surrender has never been an option for me.

14:17.815 --> 14:20.025
I understand as I also hate losing,

14:20.651 --> 14:22.194
so trust me and drop it.

14:22.820 --> 14:26.073
My intention is not to die, but to live.

15:15.664 --> 15:17.166
There are no survivors.

15:18.417 --> 15:20.544
Is the 1st Military Police Squad all gone?

15:20.628 --> 15:22.504
Yes. That's correct, sir.

15:44.985 --> 15:45.986
Could it be

15:47.571 --> 15:50.574
that it learned
how to operate the elevator?

15:51.951 --> 15:55.496
How could you allow
something like this to happen?

15:55.579 --> 15:57.039
My apologies.

15:58.624 --> 16:01.794
We were attacked out of nowhere.

16:01.877 --> 16:04.296
So, where is the specimen right now?

16:04.380 --> 16:05.631
Rest assured, sir.

16:05.714 --> 16:07.883
The elevator has already been shut down,

16:07.967 --> 16:11.553
and machine gun crews are stationed
in all paths to the first-level basement.

16:11.637 --> 16:15.265
We've also deployed combat units,
so the situation will be over soon.

16:15.349 --> 16:18.018
Do you know what I hate the most?

16:18.852 --> 16:20.938
Problems occurring when they shouldn't.

16:22.106 --> 16:26.235
And what I hate more than that
is failing to fix such problems.

16:26.819 --> 16:27.903
Forgive me, sir.

16:28.612 --> 16:34.159
Apologizing helplessly and pathetically
without a plan to fix the problem

16:34.243 --> 16:37.538
is what failures do, Mr. Soma.

16:41.500 --> 16:45.170
Take care of it before something
even more annoying arises.

16:45.671 --> 16:46.505
Understood?

16:46.588 --> 16:47.631
Yes, sir!

16:51.176 --> 16:52.970
We have captured an intruder, sir.

17:03.022 --> 17:04.064
Look who we have here.

17:04.148 --> 17:06.108
The young master of the Bugang Company.

17:07.526 --> 17:10.362
I have heard
that you're quite a troublemaker.

17:10.904 --> 17:12.656
It seems you're in big trouble now.

17:14.450 --> 17:16.910
Did Jang Tae-sang
of Golden Treasure tag along?

17:16.994 --> 17:18.829
This has nothing to do with them.

17:19.621 --> 17:20.706
Don't tell me…

17:23.709 --> 17:25.002
you're a rebel too?

17:28.797 --> 17:30.716
I'd rather you didn't tell my old man.

17:37.139 --> 17:40.809
Don't get smart with me.
You're in the wrong place for that.

17:41.894 --> 17:44.104
It doesn't matter whose son you are.

17:44.188 --> 17:47.357
That is to say, no one will care
should you die in here.

17:49.193 --> 17:50.235
Understood?

17:55.407 --> 17:56.825
Take him to the laboratory.

17:56.909 --> 17:57.910
Yes, sir!

18:06.710 --> 18:10.631
The timing couldn't have been better.
The hospital's funds were running short.

18:11.465 --> 18:14.760
Teach him a hard lesson,
but not enough to kill him.

18:19.264 --> 18:20.224
Get in.

18:26.396 --> 18:28.065
Open this door! Open it!

18:28.774 --> 18:29.775
Open the door.

18:31.110 --> 18:33.070
Let go!

18:33.153 --> 18:34.154
Keep still!

19:14.611 --> 19:15.445
Sir!

19:17.364 --> 19:18.198
What is it?

19:18.282 --> 19:19.950
The disease control platoon sent word.

19:20.033 --> 19:24.329
Two intruders caught on the second level
are being taken to Colonel Kato.

19:38.677 --> 19:39.511
Who are they?

19:39.595 --> 19:41.597
Intruders who have snuck
into the building.

19:56.028 --> 19:57.112
Master Jang?

19:57.196 --> 19:58.488
Is that Master Jang?

19:58.572 --> 19:59.907
That's Master Jang.

20:02.075 --> 20:03.118
Shut it!

20:10.459 --> 20:12.127
This one is coming with me.

20:13.587 --> 20:15.339
- Bring him.
- Yes, sir.

20:16.131 --> 20:18.634
Where are you taking me? What about her?

20:18.717 --> 20:19.551
Don't move!

20:22.221 --> 20:23.680
Get your hands off her!

20:25.349 --> 20:28.185
What? Is she your woman or something?

20:29.102 --> 20:30.187
Let's go.

20:30.270 --> 20:32.814
Stay where you are.
I'll find you no matter what.

20:36.526 --> 20:38.237
I'll come for you!

20:38.320 --> 20:40.113
I promise!

21:13.272 --> 21:16.775
The creature may be
more intelligent than expected.

21:18.735 --> 21:20.237
It knows how to use the elevator…

21:26.451 --> 21:29.454
and it's been more than an hour
since we lost sight of it.

21:38.005 --> 21:40.716
I wonder what it is that it's after.

21:51.393 --> 21:56.648
We just apprehended the intruders.
It seems that they've seen the specimen.

22:47.115 --> 22:50.160
Now, let's talk, shall we?

22:52.162 --> 22:54.414
Why did you sneak in here?

22:54.498 --> 22:56.416
What is your purpose?

22:58.168 --> 22:59.753
I'm looking for someone.

23:01.797 --> 23:04.383
Speaking the Joseon tongue
is prohibited, Josenjing.

23:05.092 --> 23:06.843
I order you to speak in Japanese.

23:10.097 --> 23:13.308
So it's illegal for a Joseon person
to speak the Joseon language,

23:14.935 --> 23:17.771
but it's legal for you to do
what you're doing here?

23:22.484 --> 23:23.318
Speak

23:23.902 --> 23:25.028
in

23:25.112 --> 23:27.906
Japanese.

23:28.490 --> 23:32.077
If you can't understand me,
bring someone who speaks my language.

23:34.621 --> 23:36.373
You seem more desperate, after all.

23:45.924 --> 23:49.511
Now, why don't we start over?

23:49.594 --> 23:52.764
Why did you sneak in here?

23:57.310 --> 23:58.895
What do you want to know?

23:59.771 --> 24:03.191
I'm sure you heard the news
about the Bombing of Tokyo.

24:04.025 --> 24:04.943
Well,

24:05.735 --> 24:07.404
through the grapevine, sure.

24:07.487 --> 24:08.738
That being said,

24:08.822 --> 24:12.826
I don't intend to return to Tokyo
even after the war ends.

24:13.577 --> 24:16.997
My wife and child
share an affection for Gyeongseong.

24:17.080 --> 24:18.623
They wish to keep living here.

24:19.374 --> 24:20.459
So?

24:23.503 --> 24:26.339
A settlement fund of 300 yen,
a house to live in,

24:28.425 --> 24:30.302
and a store about ten pyeong big.

24:31.303 --> 24:35.223
Provide me with these,
and I'll let you leave this place alive.

24:41.855 --> 24:44.608
Why should I agree to those terms?

24:44.691 --> 24:48.528
Because you already owe me once
for your life.

24:50.155 --> 24:52.282
May we take a look inside the cart?

25:05.295 --> 25:07.631
Is there anything else
you'd like to check?

25:08.256 --> 25:10.509
No. I apologize for the trouble,
Mr. Sachimoto.

25:12.511 --> 25:14.346
Frankly, I was quite taken aback.

25:15.096 --> 25:16.932
I knew you were here for Akiko,

25:17.933 --> 25:19.851
but I didn't expect you
to help the kids escape.

25:22.604 --> 25:24.773
Anyway, where is Myeong-ja?

25:27.025 --> 25:28.026
Give up.

25:29.486 --> 25:31.905
Leaving with her is impossible now.

25:32.864 --> 25:34.741
Your plan has failed.

25:36.576 --> 25:39.412
Why is the underground prison
filled with Joseon people?

25:40.997 --> 25:44.501
What are you doing
with those innocent women and children?

25:46.753 --> 25:49.130
And what about that horrifying creature?

25:50.423 --> 25:52.342
Why have you created such a thing?

25:53.635 --> 25:57.347
Have you actually been running
biological experiments on people?

26:00.141 --> 26:01.142
I take it…

26:03.144 --> 26:04.396
that you're rejecting my offer.

26:12.153 --> 26:13.363
What about Yoon Chae-ok?

26:14.322 --> 26:16.741
Where is the woman that was with me?

26:25.166 --> 26:26.251
That must hurt.

26:27.335 --> 26:28.545
Look at that.

26:42.225 --> 26:46.187
If you want to live,
accept my terms and save yourself!

26:46.271 --> 26:48.982
If I do leave here,
I'll be a dead man anyway.

26:50.900 --> 26:53.612
So tell me where Akiko
and Yoon Chae-ok are being kept…

26:56.364 --> 26:57.699
or we won't have a deal.

27:07.000 --> 27:08.877
Why did you come in here?

27:08.960 --> 27:11.004
What is your purpose?

27:13.882 --> 27:15.717
Answer me right now!

27:19.929 --> 27:21.306
Screw you.

27:26.561 --> 27:27.395
Come grab her.

28:03.223 --> 28:05.266
I know quite well

28:05.767 --> 28:10.689
how to deal with girls like you.

28:18.029 --> 28:19.614
Answer me, Josenjing!

28:26.037 --> 28:28.581
You may be able to violate me by force…

28:31.543 --> 28:33.920
but that doesn't mean you win.

28:36.923 --> 28:38.508
Do you still not understand?

28:38.591 --> 28:39.718
Bitch.

28:40.260 --> 28:41.678
You're dead!

28:41.761 --> 28:42.679
Stop!

28:52.105 --> 28:54.107
That's enough, First Sergeant Haneda.

28:54.190 --> 28:57.026
No, sir.
I'll make sure she learns a lesson.

28:58.403 --> 28:59.571
Can't you see?

29:00.613 --> 29:02.198
You have already lost.

30:01.883 --> 30:03.301
You were right.

30:04.761 --> 30:05.887
Just when you think

30:07.388 --> 30:09.849
the cherry blossoms
have bloomed splendidly,

30:10.892 --> 30:12.811
they begin to fall.

30:29.786 --> 30:30.787
Mrs. Nawol!

30:32.163 --> 30:34.582
What about Master Jang? Has he returned?

30:43.466 --> 30:44.551
He's not back yet?

30:53.685 --> 30:58.022
You seem to have stayed up all night.

31:00.942 --> 31:01.776
Mm-hmm.

31:03.444 --> 31:06.948
You seem to have gone out
very late last night.

31:08.408 --> 31:09.325
Yes.

31:39.939 --> 31:40.857
Have a seat.

31:44.485 --> 31:47.322
I came as soon as I received your message.

31:47.906 --> 31:50.325
What on Earth is going on?

31:52.076 --> 31:54.954
- Would you like a cup of coffee?
- Water, please.

32:00.293 --> 32:04.589
Your immature son
has gotten himself into big trouble.

32:05.423 --> 32:09.761
Last night, he was caught trespassing
in Ongseong Hospital.

32:11.638 --> 32:15.516
I am deeply ashamed
that he's caused such inconvenience.

32:15.600 --> 32:17.393
Inconvenience is an understatement.

32:20.855 --> 32:22.607
The situation is quite serious.

32:24.692 --> 32:27.528
Not only did he trespass…

32:29.906 --> 32:31.532
I heard he's a rebel.

32:34.744 --> 32:36.996
If things go wrong, your son

32:37.622 --> 32:40.166
and the Bugang Company
could both end up in danger.

33:01.020 --> 33:02.146
So, you're a rebel?

33:03.982 --> 33:07.151
What is it that you lot want?

33:08.152 --> 33:09.654
Joseon's independence.

33:10.989 --> 33:12.115
Something like that?

33:42.562 --> 33:43.980
To be honest,

33:45.148 --> 33:46.357
torture isn't my cup of tea.

33:50.528 --> 33:53.781
It's exhausting, unpleasant, and messy.

33:55.199 --> 33:56.617
It'd be much neater

33:57.702 --> 34:00.705
to put you on the table
and crack your head open

34:00.788 --> 34:02.165
or slice open your stomach.

34:16.888 --> 34:19.182
Write down the names
of your fellow intruders

34:20.391 --> 34:22.894
and the exact purpose of your intrusion.

34:24.854 --> 34:26.105
You have an hour.

34:26.939 --> 34:29.901
If you don't write it down in an hour,
you'll find yourself

34:30.943 --> 34:34.447
lying face-up on that dissection table.

34:42.455 --> 34:45.041
Joseon's independence, huh?

34:46.084 --> 34:48.086
Will you ever grow up?

34:49.003 --> 34:51.964
Are you even aware
of who the Bugang Company leeches off of?

34:53.716 --> 34:54.926
Foolish bastard.

35:09.982 --> 35:14.153
If you do reach the underground prison,
please find my little brother too.

35:14.237 --> 35:15.780
His name is Oh Sang-deok.

35:17.698 --> 35:20.701
There is a black, thumb-sized mole
next to his right ear.

35:40.179 --> 35:41.764
Why do you do that to yourself?

35:49.021 --> 35:51.649
Do you think getting wasted
will solve your problems?

35:57.155 --> 35:59.615
But I feel better now that I've thrown up.

36:01.325 --> 36:03.744
Your family called several times
from Anguk-dong.

36:06.873 --> 36:08.833
You should call it a night and go home.

36:11.961 --> 36:12.962
Tae-sang.

36:16.674 --> 36:19.051
I'm so ashamed of my father.

36:21.721 --> 36:26.100
I'm ashamed of how well-off he's become
from betraying his country.

36:27.894 --> 36:31.814
And I hate myself
for living lavishly thanks to that.

36:33.983 --> 36:37.570
The very people who groveled
at my father's feet for crumbs

36:38.654 --> 36:41.741
also pointed fingers at us
and badmouthed us behind our backs.

36:43.201 --> 36:45.119
I was so ashamed of that.

36:47.955 --> 36:50.583
That's why I beat the hell out of everyone

36:50.666 --> 36:52.335
who pointed their fingers at you.

36:55.838 --> 36:57.965
You really were something, even back then.

36:58.966 --> 37:02.303
You threw the best punches
yet refused to lead a gang of your own.

37:03.596 --> 37:06.557
Because making a living
was the most important thing for me.

37:08.643 --> 37:09.852
You're smart.

37:10.728 --> 37:12.063
You're competent.

37:14.357 --> 37:16.108
So why are you running a pawnshop?

37:17.401 --> 37:19.904
Because it suits my taste,

37:21.155 --> 37:22.281
and I'm good at it.

37:24.700 --> 37:25.826
As a man,

37:26.827 --> 37:29.580
do you truly have no desire
to serve a bigger cause?

37:30.790 --> 37:32.917
You really are persistent.

37:33.000 --> 37:35.962
Aren't you tired of saying that
for the past ten years?

37:39.423 --> 37:40.800
Well, you're a good man.

37:42.927 --> 37:46.931
My sincerity, my patriotism,
my everything.

37:49.016 --> 37:51.143
You're the only friend
who recognizes them.

37:54.563 --> 37:57.566
So join us at the Patriotic Society,
Tae-sang!

37:59.110 --> 38:02.280
Go away. The smell of alcohol
is ruining my new suit.

38:02.363 --> 38:06.742
Let's burn for our country
and go out like a passionate flame, okay?

38:08.703 --> 38:09.954
I said no.

38:10.871 --> 38:13.457
I'm going to live a long, cold life.

38:13.541 --> 38:14.458
Damn it.

38:15.376 --> 38:16.377
Hey!

38:16.460 --> 38:19.130
Tae-sang! I'm not done with you yet.

38:34.895 --> 38:38.232
I guess even the filthy-rich master
of the House of Golden Treasure

38:38.816 --> 38:40.067
can't escape prison.

38:40.818 --> 38:44.822
You didn't care to grease
some big shot's palm with your fortune?

38:45.614 --> 38:47.491
How did someone like you end up here?

38:48.492 --> 38:49.493
I know, right?

38:50.494 --> 38:52.330
This is all because of Myeong-ja.

38:52.955 --> 38:53.831
Wait, no.

38:54.498 --> 38:57.251
Not Myeong-ja. Is it because of Ishikawa?

38:57.752 --> 38:58.669
No.

38:59.587 --> 39:00.921
Maybe that wife of his?

39:02.965 --> 39:03.841
Look.

39:06.260 --> 39:07.845
Did you come in with Comrade Kwon?

39:08.763 --> 39:12.433
I don't deserve
to be mentioned alongside him.

39:13.476 --> 39:17.897
He's risking his life for a nobler cause
than rescuing a nobody like Myeong-ja.

39:22.151 --> 39:25.154
They say that human lives
are so common and trivial,

39:26.072 --> 39:28.741
yet it scares me
to think about losing mine.

39:34.413 --> 39:36.957
My goodness, I rambled on for a bit there.

39:38.000 --> 39:42.296
I should stop running my mouth
and start preparing to get out of here.

39:43.339 --> 39:44.757
What do you mean?

39:45.883 --> 39:47.301
How are you going to escape?

39:50.346 --> 39:51.514
I'm Jang Tae-sang.

39:52.181 --> 39:55.393
Did you really think
the filthy-rich master of Golden Treasure

39:55.476 --> 39:57.603
came in here
without greasing anyone's palm?

40:00.815 --> 40:04.110
From now on, grant me these three things.

40:05.903 --> 40:09.073
First, send word to Mrs. Nawol
of the House of Golden Treasure.

40:18.082 --> 40:18.999
Hello?

40:20.000 --> 40:20.835
Pardon?

40:21.335 --> 40:22.920
Yes, this is Mrs. Nawol speaking.

40:23.003 --> 40:24.755
This is a message from Master Jang.

40:25.548 --> 40:26.549
Listen carefully.

40:29.009 --> 40:29.927
Go ahead.

40:31.679 --> 40:33.264
What's your second request?

40:33.848 --> 40:36.767
Remove all guards and sentries
from the prison.

40:36.851 --> 40:39.019
You two, follow me.

40:39.687 --> 40:40.688
Right now, sir?

40:42.982 --> 40:45.776
It's about the specimen
on the fourth-level basement.

40:45.860 --> 40:47.403
Shut up and follow me!

40:49.071 --> 40:50.072
Yes, sir.

40:52.741 --> 40:54.869
Hey, you!

40:55.494 --> 40:56.328
You too.

40:56.412 --> 40:57.455
Yes, sir.

41:23.022 --> 41:24.315
Let us come with you!

41:24.398 --> 41:25.357
Take us with you.

41:25.441 --> 41:28.277
Master Jang, don't abandon us.
Take us too!

41:28.861 --> 41:30.905
Save us, Master Jang. Save us!

41:30.988 --> 41:32.573
Save us, Master Jang.

41:36.994 --> 41:38.787
- Master Jang…
- Just wait 30 minutes.

41:39.455 --> 41:40.706
I'll be back.

41:40.789 --> 41:42.917
How do you expect us to believe that?

41:43.000 --> 41:45.044
What if you don't come back?

41:45.127 --> 41:47.463
You seem to have a bit of a trust issue.

41:51.050 --> 41:52.593
I promise to come back,

41:52.676 --> 41:56.430
so don't do anything
and stay put until I do.

41:57.348 --> 41:58.641
Okay.

41:59.934 --> 42:02.770
- Master Jang.
- Master Jang! Where are you going?

42:04.522 --> 42:07.024
The third request is too much.

42:07.691 --> 42:08.984
You could die.

42:09.068 --> 42:11.570
I'll decide for myself
whether I die or not.

42:13.781 --> 42:14.782
Yoon Chae-ok.

42:15.824 --> 42:16.992
Where is she?

42:23.332 --> 42:24.208
Do you need this?

42:43.727 --> 42:44.728
Thank you.

42:48.983 --> 42:50.734
I don't speak the Joseon tongue.

42:52.152 --> 42:53.988
I was stationed in Manchuria.

42:54.655 --> 42:56.365
With the disease control platoon?

42:58.450 --> 43:00.911
Did you bring that creature
from there as well?

43:03.622 --> 43:04.456
You…

43:08.127 --> 43:09.461
Are you with the Resistance?

43:09.545 --> 43:13.048
I was on the search for my mother
who'd gone missing ten years ago.

43:14.842 --> 43:16.760
While searching for her,

43:17.970 --> 43:20.639
I found out what you people did
on Manwol Island.

43:24.435 --> 43:28.105
I never expected
to hear about Manwol Island here.

43:28.188 --> 43:31.442
Why did you bring the creature
all the way to Gyeongseong?

43:34.111 --> 43:37.031
Because of my sincere curiosity
and passion as a scientist

43:38.282 --> 43:40.534
and my affection for my creation.

43:41.535 --> 43:42.536
You know,

43:43.495 --> 43:45.080
for those complex reasons.

43:56.133 --> 43:57.134
By the way,

43:59.178 --> 44:01.347
have we met before?

44:04.391 --> 44:05.392
I'm certain

44:06.852 --> 44:08.937
that I know those eyes from somewhere.

44:17.154 --> 44:18.197
Tell me,

44:19.782 --> 44:22.201
what was the name of your lost mother?

44:23.661 --> 44:24.787
Choi Seong-sim.

44:28.082 --> 44:28.916
Seishin.

44:49.103 --> 44:50.187
Your name.

44:50.771 --> 44:51.772
Choi…

44:52.940 --> 44:54.066
Seong-sim.

44:59.947 --> 45:00.989
Seishin.

45:11.417 --> 45:12.334
But

45:13.544 --> 45:15.671
why do you ask for my mother's name?

45:20.884 --> 45:23.762
How was it in person? My specimen.

45:25.723 --> 45:26.807
It was horrifying.

45:27.891 --> 45:28.934
Did you perhaps

45:29.601 --> 45:33.397
feel anything else
when you faced the specimen?

45:34.106 --> 45:35.107
Not really.

45:36.567 --> 45:38.944
I was too busy running away
to feel anything else.

45:39.945 --> 45:42.364
It seemed like it existed only to attack.

45:49.580 --> 45:51.373
Now it's your turn to answer.

45:52.875 --> 45:55.127
Why did you ask for my mother's name?

45:55.878 --> 45:56.879
Do you…

45:58.881 --> 46:00.382
know my mother, by any chance?

46:07.723 --> 46:09.475
Your Japanese is quite good.

46:11.477 --> 46:13.562
Why did you suffer needlessly back there?

46:13.645 --> 46:15.981
Even if I had answered in Japanese…

46:18.484 --> 46:19.777
nothing would've changed.

46:22.738 --> 46:23.739
I see.

47:20.295 --> 47:21.922
- Take her away.
- Yes, sir.

47:30.639 --> 47:33.350
Don't touch her
without my explicit permission.

47:35.352 --> 47:36.979
If you disobey my orders,

47:37.938 --> 47:40.315
you will be demoted to an infantryman.

47:41.358 --> 47:43.694
- Do I make myself clear?
- Yes, sir.

48:02.296 --> 48:03.505
Just wait.

48:03.589 --> 48:07.509
I'm going to kill you with my own hands.

48:09.344 --> 48:11.096
I'd like to see you try it.

48:13.265 --> 48:15.684
Inferior soldier.

48:16.560 --> 48:18.145
"Inferior soldier"?

48:19.062 --> 48:20.314
"Inferior soldier"!

48:20.397 --> 48:21.648
"Inferior soldier."

48:22.733 --> 48:23.859
Shut up.

48:25.152 --> 48:26.737
Do you have a death wish?

48:31.575 --> 48:33.660
Officer Asano would like to see you, sir.

49:29.549 --> 49:33.720
My son may be immature at times,
but I've no brother and he's the only son.

49:33.804 --> 49:35.514
He is to carry on the family name.

49:36.807 --> 49:40.018
Please have mercy
and forgive him just this once.

49:43.105 --> 49:44.731
I beg of you, Dr. Ichiro!

49:47.234 --> 49:48.986
You put me in a difficult position.

49:52.656 --> 49:54.366
We'll see what happens.

50:04.501 --> 50:06.128
Did you put in the right amount?

50:06.712 --> 50:07.629
Yes, sir.

50:08.130 --> 50:09.965
I did as you instructed.

50:16.388 --> 50:20.058
He's a fickle man.
We will need to prepare alternative plans.

50:21.268 --> 50:22.185
Yes, sir.

50:23.103 --> 50:25.022
Why don't you leave that up to us?

50:32.654 --> 50:34.865
Aren't you
from the House of Golden Treasure?

50:35.532 --> 50:36.450
Yes.

50:36.533 --> 50:41.038
And we just got ahold of a plan
to save Master Kwon.

52:08.917 --> 52:15.924
I MISS YOU, CHAE-OK
MY DEAR DAUGHTER

52:31.481 --> 52:33.900
Have we met before?

52:34.484 --> 52:36.361
I know those eyes from somewhere.

52:38.280 --> 52:41.408
What was the name of your lost mother?

53:01.511 --> 53:02.512
I want

53:04.139 --> 53:04.973
to live.

53:10.395 --> 53:11.438
I want to live…

53:16.651 --> 53:17.944
so I can see you.

53:21.698 --> 53:22.908
My dear daughter.

53:25.911 --> 53:29.748
I MISS YOU, CHAE-OK
MY DEAR DAUGHTER

53:29.831 --> 53:31.875
Chae-ok.

54:04.824 --> 54:06.451
Mother.

54:15.418 --> 54:16.670
I'm starving.

54:17.170 --> 54:18.421
What time is it?

54:19.047 --> 54:20.799
We still have an hour left.

54:40.402 --> 54:42.112
- It's the real deal!
- What is it?

54:42.904 --> 54:43.905
Caramel?

54:44.447 --> 54:47.242
Why is something so valuable
rolling around in here?

54:47.909 --> 54:49.160
There's another one here.

55:04.801 --> 55:06.136
Hey, are you all right?

55:14.311 --> 55:16.813
What's wrong? Are you hurt? Ms. Yoon!

55:23.653 --> 55:24.696
What happened?

55:25.488 --> 55:26.489
What's wrong?

55:28.992 --> 55:30.785
My mother was here.

55:31.828 --> 55:32.912
Your mother?

55:35.123 --> 55:37.751
I MISS YOU, CHAE-OK
MY DEAR DAUGHTER

55:39.169 --> 55:40.170
Your mother was here?

55:40.879 --> 55:42.505
She might still be here.

55:49.763 --> 55:53.433
I get where you're coming from,
but we're in a bad spot. Why don't we…

55:57.103 --> 55:59.189
You move according to your plan.

56:00.231 --> 56:01.733
I'll move on my own from now on.

56:01.816 --> 56:03.735
Where will you even go?

56:03.818 --> 56:06.488
Now that I know my mother is here,
I can't just leave.

56:08.281 --> 56:09.491
I'm going to find her.

56:12.243 --> 56:13.411
Look.

56:13.495 --> 56:16.039
This place is swarming
with Japanese soldiers.

56:16.122 --> 56:19.501
They are armed and searching for us.
And that's not all.

56:19.584 --> 56:22.796
A mysterious creature is wreaking havoc.
What can you do by yourself?

56:23.880 --> 56:27.092
Listen to me.
Why don't we get out of here for today?

56:27.842 --> 56:30.428
I'll look for another way
to find out about your mother.

56:31.763 --> 56:34.849
What are you going to do
if you run into the creature again?

56:34.933 --> 56:37.060
How do you plan to fight it on your own?

56:37.143 --> 56:38.937
And should something bad happen--

56:48.905 --> 56:50.031
Thank you.

56:54.828 --> 56:57.330
And I'm sorry
I can't stay with you until the end.

57:16.808 --> 57:17.976
Must you really go?

57:19.144 --> 57:20.145
Ten years.

57:23.606 --> 57:27.026
For ten years, I've looked everywhere
in search of my mother.

57:29.362 --> 57:30.947
And now I know she's here.

57:34.492 --> 57:35.785
So I have to find her.

57:50.467 --> 57:51.843
Stay alive.

59:17.262 --> 59:23.309
HOUSE OF GOLDEN TREASURE

59:31.067 --> 59:38.074
HOUSE OF GOLDEN TREASURE
MASTER JANG TAE-SANG

59:53.256 --> 59:57.093
SLEUTH YOON CHAE-OK

01:00:06.644 --> 01:00:09.272
SLEUTH YOON JUNG-WON

01:00:12.025 --> 01:00:14.402
TO FIND LEE IN-HYEOK
OF THE PATRIOTIC SOCIETY

01:00:38.885 --> 01:00:40.928
What? Where did everybody go?

01:00:54.984 --> 01:00:55.985
You.

01:00:57.904 --> 01:00:59.822
You know who Choi Seong-sim is, don't you?

01:01:04.077 --> 01:01:05.203
Where is she?

01:01:13.920 --> 01:01:14.962
Answer me!

01:01:18.132 --> 01:01:19.884
Where is my mother right now?
